// task submission with backpressure, panic recovery, graceful shutdown, and
// deterministic result delivery.
//
// Public API:
//
//   - NewPool(capacity int, workers int) *Pool
//     Creates a new pool with the given queue capacity and number of workers.
//     capacity must be >= 0; workers must be >= 1.
//
//   - (*Pool).Submit(ctx context.Context, task func() (interface{}, error)) error
//     Submits a task to the pool. Returns an error if the pool is closed or
//     the context is canceled before the task can be enqueued.
//
//   - (*Pool).Wait(ctx context.Context) error
//     Waits for all submitted tasks to complete. Returns an error if the
//     context is canceled.
//
//   - (*Pool).Close()
//     Initiates graceful shutdown. No new tasks can be submitted after Close
//     is called. Existing tasks in the queue will still be processed.
//     Close is idempotent.
//
//   - (*Pool).Shutdown(ctx context.Context) error
//     Like Close but waits for all tasks to complete or context cancellation.
//     Returns an error if the context is canceled before all tasks finish.
//
// Concurrency invariants:
//   - At most `workers` goroutines execute tasks concurrently.
//   - The queue holds at most `capacity` pending tasks.
//   - Submit blocks (with backpressure) when the queue is full until space is
//     available or the context is canceled.
//   - Panics in tasks are recovered and converted to errors.
//   - All goroutines are properly cleaned up on Close/Shutdown.
